notes='''### 043-N1 — Conditions and explicit withdrawal

The page continues “caractérisée” from 042 and gives four proposed conditions on the quotient topology. Its upper marginal correction says “C’est faux, ça implique (i) (ii) (iii) (iv), mais ces conditions ne suffisent nullement, voir plus bas ! v. 48”. Another note says the final-topology condition was forgotten on page 31. The right note translates the conditions to S and says the discussion is independent of the ultra-topological hypothesis. The proof of (a,b,c) begins by asserting uniqueness of the pair description and closed-set stability. Manuscript page 42; references 31 and 48 are his manuscript page numbers, not new dates.

### 043-N2 — Decisions guided by the mathematics, settled in ink

Condition (i) has tilde τ restricted to J′, with a visible wave, not H’s bar. In (ii), the equality U′=I′∖J′ is written immediately after the restriction without separating punctuation; it remains as written. In (iii), the codomain is U=S∖T despite the preceding quotient notation; no inferred I∖J replaces it. The finality note has a doubtful double prime on the first topology and an unprimed topology on T. The author’s own retraction is decisive evidence of his change of view, not a proof supplied by this transcription. The four-condition characterization is not independently proved or refuted here.

### 043-N3 — Proof status

The page calls arbitrary-intersection stability “clair” and finite-union stability “idem”; it also asserts arbitrary-union stability under the two ultra-topological hypotheses. These are recorded as assertions. The constructed-family argument already checked in 040-N2/041-N3 is relevant background, but no new proof check is claimed on this sheet. The last reference reads d)/a) uncertain from a short low ascender; mathematical expectation does not remove that uncertainty.'''
